  "notes": "Cool, low-register, laid-back — and the pocket is the parameter. The research says the kick sits back and the vocal is delivered low and behind the beat, so this entry loosens `quantizeStrength` to 0.84, adds real `timingJitterMs` on the kick and clap, and pushes the snare 6 ms late with `offGridMs`. Nothing else on this axis is authored behind the grid. `melody.articulation` is `legato` for the drawled tails and the density band is the second-sparsest here. The 808 glides specifically between root and b7, which is why `slideIntervals` is weighted to `m7` — a movement no other entry in this batch uses. ⚠ `confidence` medium, per the research. The INFERRED parameters are the exact timing figures: \"laid-back kick placement\" and \"delivered low and behind the beat\" are qualitative, and 6 ms plus a 0.84 quantize is this author's reading of how far back that is. ⚠ Two-chord beds means `maxChords` 3 and a `2_bars_per_chord`-led harmonic rhythm; the chord part's 55-output floor is carried by `chordDurationBeats` [4,12] rather than by families the records do not play. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
